  "title": "AWS CodeBuild Now Supports Cross-Account Resource Sharing",
  "text": "AWS CodeBuild now allows you to securely share your CodeBuild resources, such as Projects and Report Groups , across AWS accounts or within your AWS organization. Previously, you couldn't share your build details or test reports generated in one account with other AWS accounts. AWS CodeBuild now allows you to securely share your CodeBuild resources, such as Projects and Report Groups , across AWS accounts or within your AWS organization. Previously, you couldn't share your build details or test reports generated in one account with other AWS accounts. You can now use AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM) to securely share your AWS CodeBuild Projects or Report Groups across your AWS accounts or within your AWS organization. By using AWS RAM to share your CodeBuild resources, you no longer need to create duplicate resources in each of your AWS accounts. This reduces operational overhead while maintaining the benefits of a multi-account strategy. To learn more about working with a shared Project or a Report Group , visit our documentation. To get started with CodeBuild, visit our product page or the CodeBuild console .",
